 ### Deformation Transfer via ACAP
-This method transfers mesh deformation to 3D Gaussians by calculating vertex transformations using ACAP, interpolating them via barycentric coordinates, and averaging transformations across 8 bound faces. It sets itself apart by using Gaussian-centric binding and averaging operations for robust deformation transfer. Choose for transferring cage or box deformations to Gaussians.
+This method transfers mesh deformation to 3D Gaussians by calculating vertex transformations using ACAP, interpolating them via barycentric coordinates, and averaging transformations across 8 bound faces [S2]. It sets itself apart by using Gaussian-centric binding and averaging operations for robust deformation transfer [S2]. Choose for transferring cage or box deformations to Gaussians [S2]. For each of the 8 BBX corners (index $i$) and 3 triangle vertices (index $j$), calculate offset $\Delta_{ji}$, rotation $R_{ji}$, and shear $S_{ji}$ using polar decomposition of transformation matrix $D_{ji}$ [S2]. Average the transformations ($R, S, \Delta$) across the 8 bound faces to get global transformation for the Gaussian [S2]. Formulas: $\Delta_i = u\Delta_{1i} + v\Delta_{2i} + w\Delta_{3i} = u(V'_{i1} - V_{i1}) + v(V'_{i2} - V_{i2}) + w(V'_{i3} - V_{i3})$, where $u,v,w$ are barycentric coordinates [S2]. $R_i = u \log(R_{i1}) + v \log(R_{i2}) + w \log(R_{i3})$, and $S_i = uS_{i1} + vS_{i2} + wS_{i3}$ [S2]. $R' = \exp(\frac{1}{8} \sum_{i=1}^{8} R_i)$, $S' = \frac{1}{8} \sum_{i=1}^{8} S_i$, $\Sigma' = R' S' \Sigma (R' S')^T$, $\mu' = \mu + \frac{1}{8} \sum_{i=1}^{8} \Delta_i$ [S2]. $G'(x) = \exp(-\frac{1}{2} (x-\mu')^T (\Sigma')^{-1} (x-\mu'))$, where $G'$ is the updated Gaussian kernel [S2].
 
